section: compiler
synopsis: Fix lookups of non-recursive lets in CoreMap
description:
  ``CoreMap`` stored a non-recursive ``let`` under one key path and looked
  it up under a different key path. When a map held two different
  expressions, each lookup of an expression with a non-recursive ``let``
  or join point failed. Thus CSE did not share identical bindings, and the
  pattern-match checker could report spurious non-exhaustive matches for
  guards or view patterns with equal expressions. ``CoreMap`` and
  ``eqCoreExpr`` also ignore the multiplicities of binders.
